        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.15.0 — 2026-07-17</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Registrations sorted by surname</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The signup table now leads with <strong>Last name</strong> and is sorted by it. It was newest-first, which is the order they arrived in and no order at all when you're looking for a person. Sorted with Swiss collation, so <strong>Dürig</strong> sits between Demir and Mayer rather than after Z</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>"Email sent to …" is now a toast</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The confirmation used to be a few pixels of grey text in the row, gone on the next redraw. It now appears as a message in the corner, showing the address the server actually sent to. On a failure it says <em>the result is recorded and only the email failed</em>, and stays longer</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>SVRZ Wohnort: looked up, not invented</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Postcode and town are filled from the member records</strong> when a signup didn't give them. The form asked for "Adresse" in a single box and most people read that as "street": 16 of 25 gave no town at all</li>
              <li>Where nothing is known — not from the signup, not from the members — the list says <strong>"Zürich"</strong> with no postcode. That's a guess and deliberately the last resort: only about 70% of members live in Zürich. The lookup found <strong>Wädenswil</strong> and <strong>Stallikon</strong> among people who'd otherwise have been labelled Zürich</li>
              <li><strong>The export says so first.</strong> Missing licence numbers and guessed towns are listed for confirmation before it downloads — a guessed town looks exactly like data once it's in a spreadsheet cell</li>
              <li>The form has since been split into <strong>Strasse / PLZ / Ort</strong> and is read directly. Older signups are still parsed as before</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.14.0 — 2026-07-17</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Scoresheet column: a coloured icon instead of a tick</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The tick is now a <strong>Matchblatt icon whose colour is the state</strong>: grey — no scoresheet, green — one is on file, blue — a correction exists on top of it. A legend under the table explains the colours</li>
              <li><strong>The icon is clickable even when grey.</strong> Scoresheets also arrive by email or on paper, and the column had nowhere to put one. There is now "Upload scoresheet (received directly)", filed as the participant's own sheet rather than as a correction to nothing</li>
              <li>If a scoresheet is already there, uploading one directly is refused: to change an existing sheet you upload a correction, which keeps both and records who made it</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Download a scoresheet</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>New in the menu: <strong>Download scoresheet</strong> — saved as <code>schreiberpruefung_337646.pdf</code>, the same name the SVRZ zip uses</li>
              <li><strong>Opening a sheet now always gives a PDF</strong>, whatever the participant's phone produced. Previously a phone photo opened as a bare image and "save as" offered a cryptic blob id as the filename. The stored original is left untouched</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.13.0 — 2026-07-17</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Exam result: Yes / No — with an email and a note</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The "Exam passed" checkbox has given way to two buttons: <strong>Yes</strong> and <strong>No</strong>. A checkbox knows two states and the question has three — passed, not passed, and nobody has looked yet. The third is the most common one, and it must not show up on the SVRZ Teilnehmerliste as "Nicht bestanden"</li>
              <li>Both answers ask first, then automatically email the participant the result. The confirmation box takes an optional <strong>note</strong> — what was missing, or what to watch out for — and it travels with the email</li>
              <li>Clicking the answer that is already set clears the result back to "not decided yet" — with no email, since there is no longer a result to report</li>
              <li>The Teilnehmerliste now reads "Bestanden" or "Nicht bestanden"; anyone not yet assessed stays blank</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Upload a corrected scoresheet</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The green tick in the "Exam uploaded" column now opens a menu: show the scoresheet, <strong>upload a corrected one</strong> — and, once one exists, view both side by side</li>
              <li>The participant's own sheet is never overwritten: it is what they submitted, and the correction sits on top of it. The menu shows <strong>who</strong> corrected it and when, and the tick turns amber, so corrected rows are visible at a glance</li>
              <li>The result email carries the corrected sheet as a PDF attachment, when one has been uploaded</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>SVRZ export: scoresheets as PDFs, named after the licence number</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>In the zip, scoresheets are now called <code>schreiberpruefung_337646.pdf</code> — after the licence number rather than the person. If someone's number is missing, the export says so before it downloads, since SVRZ needs it on the list anyway</li>
              <li>Phone photos are converted to PDF for the export, so SVRZ receives PDFs throughout. Where a correction exists, it goes into the zip instead of the original</li>
