          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.9.0 — 2026-07-13</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Admin: Excel export for scorer courses — now including the tracking columns</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The scorer-course registrations view gained an Excel export next to the existing TSV one: a real .xlsx with a frozen, bold header row, a filter on every column, and the present / exam-sent / exam-passed ticks written as true Excel booleans so they can be filtered and counted. Licence numbers stay text, so a leading zero is never swallowed</li>
              <li>Fixed: both exports silently dropped everything KSCW tracks itself — present, exam sent, exam passed, SV licence and notes. The export was built from the sign-up form's answers alone, while the tracking lives in a separate collection, so an SV licence entered by an admin (the usual case for a new referee) never made it into the file. Exports now carry exactly what the table shows, including edits made just before exporting</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.8.1 — 2026-07-09</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Admin: scorer registration details — one field per row</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The expanded sign-up (the ▸ detail view in the scorer-course registrations table) now lists each field on its own line — date, phone, email, address, birthdate, language, participation, KSCW membership, club/team and notes stack vertically instead of wrapping several per line, so a registrant's details are easier to scan</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.8.0 — 2026-07-09</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Admin: scorer-course registrations — compact rows, SVRZ pre-fill & bulk email</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The registrations table now shows a compact row — first name, last name, the present / exam-sent / exam-passed toggles, the licence field and delete — so it fits on screen without sideways scrolling. A ▸ arrow (or a click on the name) expands the full sign-up: phone, email, address, birthdate, participation, team, notes and everything else, plus the editable tracking note</li>
              <li>The SV licence field is pre-filled from the sign-up's "SVRZ Licence Number" answer when the applicant provided one and it hasn't been tracked yet (a value you've already entered always wins). Saves as before, only when you edit it</li>
              <li>New Send email button: it reveals a per-registrant checkbox (all selected by default, with a select-all box), then opens your default mail program with the chosen participants pre-addressed — handy for "message everyone on this course"</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.7.0 — 2026-07-09</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Admin: scorer-course registrations, inline with attendance & exam tracking</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The website admin (/admin) now keeps the open section in the address bar (e.g. /admin/?tab=scorer_courses), so a tab can be bookmarked or shared and the browser Back/Forward buttons move between sections</li>
              <li>A scorer course's sign-ups now open inline (no pop-up) as an editable table. For each registrant you can tick present, exam sent and exam passed, add a note, and fill in a Swiss Volley licence number when it was missing from the sign-up. Changes save immediately</li>
              <li>The sign-up data itself stays read-only; the tracking is stored on our side (the form tool has no place for it)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.6.0 — 2026-07-09</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Basketball registration: full Swiss Basketball document flow</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The form now asks basketball applicants which licensing situation applies — new licence, transfer from another Swiss club, coming from a club abroad, or returning to Switzerland — and requests exactly the documents Swiss Basketball's procedure needs. Previously only "new player" was handled, so transfers had no way to submit their release letter (Freibrief)</li>
              <li>Depending on the situation, the Freibrief, the FIBA parental consent (U18) and an optional school-enrolment certificate are collected, each with an auto-filled template to download. Whether the U18 documents are required is derived from the date of birth</li>
              <li>Documents that don't apply to your situation are never shown and never block submission; the optional school certificate never blocks it either</li>
              <li>The licence application (Lizenzantrag) template was updated to the current version</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.5.2 — 2026-07-07</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Registration: reliable team loading</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>On basketball/volleyball registrations the team list was fetched only after sport and role were chosen; if that request failed on a flaky connection the list stayed empty with no error, and the form couldn't be submitted ("no team selected"). Teams now load when the form opens, and a "Try again" prompt appears if it fails</li>
              <li>Mixed youth categories (MU8, MU10, U12) were shown only to male applicants — girls now see them too</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.5.1 — 2026-07-06</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Calendar: numbered referees</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Referees in the game popup are now listed individually as "1st referee" / "2nd referee"</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.5.0 — 2026-07-06</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Calendar: full game details</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The game popup in the calendar now shows the league, the official game number and (volleyball) the assigned referees</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Scorer courses: 2026 materials</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The course materials (PDF) and course presentation (PPT) now link to the current 2026 files — two cards instead of four</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.4.0 — 2026-07-06</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Scorer courses: fully editable in the admin panel</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The venue, the "Hosted by … / Powered by …" note and the course duration (length of the calendar entry) were hardcoded. They are now editable per course in the admin panel — leaving a field empty hides that line on the public course card</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.3.1 — 2026-06-30</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Calendar: instant month navigation</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The calendar reloaded its data on every month change, briefly flashing a loading bar. All games and hall closures now load once when the page opens, so switching between months is instant — no refetch</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.3.0 — 2026-06-26</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Youth: up-to-date sign-up status</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>On the basketball youth page, the team cards now always show the current status — “Open for players” with a contact link, or “Team full” with a waiting list — updating automatically as soon as something changes</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.2.2 — 2026-06-26</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Registration fixed</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The membership form silently refused to submit for younger applicants (under 23/25) — with no error message at all. The cause was a hidden required field; sign-ups now go through</li>
              <li>The confirmation ("thank you for signing up") wasn't shown after a successful submit — it now appears correctly</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.2.1 — 2026-06-25</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Registration form security check fixed</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>On a long registration (e.g. basketball, with documents to download and upload) the security check (captcha) could expire and silently block submitting. It now refreshes automatically while the form is open, with a clear "please re-confirm" message if it ever lapses</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.2.0 — 2026-06-25</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Hall closures in the calendar</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The calendar now also shows "hall closed" days — school holidays, public holidays and hall closures (e.g. for tournaments). One marker per day with the affected halls; a toggle at the top shows or hides them</li>
              <li>Calendar subscription fixed and extended: the subscribe / download link works again, and hall closures can now be subscribed to as a source (events were previously dropped from the subscription by mistake)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.1.1 — 2026-06-24</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Calendar &amp; event dates fixed</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>All-day events (e.g. the Photoday) showed up one day too early in the calendar and on the homepage. Dates are now always read in Swiss time (Europe/Zurich), so they land on the correct day no matter where you are</li>
              <li>News dates are likewise pinned to Swiss time</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.1.0 — 2026-06-20</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Standings by season</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Team-page standings now have a season picker — current tables, last season's final standings (2024/25 added back) and the archive</li>
              <li>For a season Swiss Volley hasn't published yet, a short note appears instead of an empty table</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.0.0 — 2026-06-19</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Site &amp; navigation</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Bilingual German / English site with a single canonical URL per page and a language toggle that remembers your choice</li>
              <li>Live on the club's own domain, kscw.ch</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Teams</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Dynamic team pages (volleyball and basketball) with live data from Directus: games, rankings, roster, photos and a weekly training summary from the real hall schedule</li>
              <li>Promotion / relegation colour bands on rankings, season-stable team matching that survives the yearly rollover, and a basketball youth section with live coaches and training times</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Games, scoreboard &amp; calendar</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Homepage game rows and a game detail modal with sets, referees and venue</li>
              <li>A scoreboard with Absolute / Per-Game toggle, and a live calendar with event tooltips and detail modals</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Registration &amp; membership</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>A unified online registration form for volleyball, basketball and passive memberships, with ID upload, PDF pre-fill of the licence forms and Turnstile spam protection</li>
              <li>An admin registrations tab with approve / reject workflow, ClubDesk CSV export and automatic confirmation emails</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>News, events &amp; courses</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Club news on the homepage and a news page with RSS, calendar events with sign-up links and live submission counts, and scorer courses with an „add to calendar“ button</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Contact &amp; feedback</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>A central contact form that reaches the right coaches without exposing their email addresses</li>
              <li>A feedback form (bug / feature / feedback) with screenshot upload that opens a GitHub issue automatically</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Content pages</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>About us with club history and a map, the board as an org chart, regulations with SVRZ embeds, sponsors, imprint and privacy policy</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Design &amp; polish</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Animated hero, scroll-progress bar, card spotlight, 3D-tilt team cards and section-aware sparkle effects — all respecting „reduce motion“</li>
              <li>Swiss dd.mm.yyyy dates and HH:MM times throughout, with a dark / light theme</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Admin &amp; infrastructure</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>A hidden admin area with per-person area permissions enforced on the server, not just hidden in the UI</li>
              <li>Built on Astro 6 with a Directus REST backend, Cloudflare Pages hosting and hardened CSP / security headers</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
